  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">220000114 Contribution to the Global Financing Facility 2023-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Financing Facility (GFF) serves as a funding instrument for the UN&apos;s Global Strategy for Women&apos;s, Children&apos;s and Adolescents&apos; Health (2016-2030) under the Every Woman, Every Child (EWEC) initiative. The trust fund aims to leverage more IDA- and IBRD- but also domestic resources and private funds for Reproductive Maternal Neonatal Child and Adolescent Health (hereafter RMNCHA). In addition, efficient use of resources at country level is being pursued. The initiative lies with national governments but GFF, as well as World Bank and the alliance partners provide strategic and technical advice. Through this financing, the Netherlands continues its contribution to the GFF Trustfund, to align with the GFF strategy which ends in 2025. The Dutch focus will continue to be on SRHR, inclusiveness, civil society involvement and gender equality. This BEMO is a continuation of the contribution documented in activity 4000001934.</narrative>
  </description>
